#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""news-brief — tech & politics news, twice a day.

  news-brief              fetch the news, write the summary and open the page now
  news-brief --open       open the latest edition (what clicking the notification does)
  news-brief --build      build an edition without opening it (prints the page's path)
  news-brief --scheduled  what the systemd timer runs (7:28 and 20:28): build the edition, then
                          deliver it on the half hour (or once you've unlocked) as one notification:
                          "Your morning news is ready, want to see it?" Clicking it opens the page.

The page has a short summary at the top (written by Claude through the `claude` CLI, so it uses
your Claude subscription) and every story it was written from below, grouped into Tech and
Politics, each linking to the outlet's article.

Settings: ~/.config/news-brief/config.toml (feeds, model, how many stories; see config.example.toml).
Editions: ~/.local/share/news-brief/ (the last 30 are kept). Log: ~/.cache/news-brief/log.
"""
